title: Tidbits: Photos
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

A recipe's or ingredient's `photo` field names a separate tiddler titled `<Title> (photo)`.  The photo tiddler holds either embedded image data or a `_canonical_uri` pointing to an external image.

Photos add visual richness, but sourcing and attributing public images takes effort.  The <$button class="tc-btn-invisible tc-tiddlylink"><$action-setfield $tiddler="$:/state/tab-1749438307" text="$:/community/recipes/ControlPanel/Recipes"/><$action-navigate $to="$:/ControlPanel"/>Recipes tab</$button> of the Control Panel offers three modes:

* **Don't use photos** — edit forms hide their photo section, and the Recipe Box dashboard shows plain text lists instead of thumbnails.
* **Use my own photos** (default) — edit forms show the photo controls but collapse the attribution fields behind a disclosure; a click expands them if you want to add credit.
* **Use public photos with attribution** — edit forms expand the attribution fields by default, since you'll want to fill them in for every photo.

Recipe and ingredient view templates always display any photos that are attached, regardless of mode.
